      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rockwood Mills, founded by former Roane Iron employee James Tarwater in 1905, began producing hosiery in the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockwood%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pig iron shipped from Rockwood by river reached Knoxville and Chattanooga rolling mills, fueling early railroad construction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockwood%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1880s Roane Iron tried steel production at a Chattanooga mill, but low‑quality Walden Ridge ore forced abandonment in 1889.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockwood%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rockwood incorporated in 1890 and banned alcohol sales in 1903, yet a “jug train” from Chattanooga kept liquor flowing until statewide prohibition in 1909.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rockwood%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Rockwood sits between the Cumberland Plateau’s Walden Ridge and Watts Bar Lake, offering dramatic valley views that line I‑40 just before the plateau’s edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
